    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d803">

                <pb facs="0821" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg815"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.24/161</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs (Alling)</hi><anchor n="84" xml:id="d803-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-03">July 3, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Greek Prime Minister will return to Washington on July 9, and desires to sign
                    the master Lend-Lease Agreement the following day. We are informed by TA<anchor
                        n="85" xml:id="d803-f2"/> and TD<anchor n="86" xml:id="d803-f3"/> that those
                    Divisions know of no reason why the ceremony should not take place at that
                    time.</p>
                <p>If you approve, we shall request the Treaty Division to have the document ready
                    for signature on the morning of July 10.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d803-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul H. Alling</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d803-f1" n="84" type="source" xml:id="d803-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Secretary of State who marked it “OK”, and to the Under
                    Secretary of State who noted on the margin: “Yes—the President is in
                    accord.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d803-f2" n="85" xml:id="d803-f2-content">
                <p>Division of Commercial Policy and Agreements.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d803-f3" n="86" xml:id="d803-f3-content">
                <p>Treaty Division.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d803-f4" n="87" xml:id="d803-f4-content">
                <p>Agreement signed July 10, 1942. For text, see Executive Agreement Series No. 260,
                    or 56 Stat. (pt. 2) 1559. For joint statement by President Roosevelt and the
                    King of Greece, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>,
                    July 11, 1942, p. 601; for press release issued by the Department July 10,
                    including text of agreement, see <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
